<title>UK: Total aluminium stocks rose in January - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Total aluminium stocks rose in January - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, rose to 3.149 million tonnes at the end of January 1997, compared with 3.138 million in December and 3.701 million in January 1996, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>But unwrought metal stocks fell to 1.662 million tonnes versus 1.691 million and 2.119 million, respectively.</p>
<p>Today's data includes inventory figures from China and Yugoslavia (Montenegro), the IPAI added.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Jan'97   Dec'96    Jan'96</p>
<p>    Africa		    70	 71	 105</p>
<p>    North America	1,461    1,460     1,687</p>
<p>    Latin America	  163	158	 212</p>
<p>    Asia		     183	173	 177</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,139    1,139     1,370</p>
<p>    Oceania		  133	137	 150</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   Jan'97    Dec'96    Jan'96</p>
<p>    Africa		    22	 24	  55</p>
<p>    North America	  644	673	 840</p>
<p>    Latin America	  117	110	 171</p>
<p>    Asia		     142	143	 153</p>
<p>    Europe		   643	638	 786</p>
<p>    Oceania		   94	103	 114</p>
<p>--London Newsroom 44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
